xcluding telephone sets or base stations); machines for the reception, conversion and transmission or regeneration of voice, images or other data, including switching and routing apparatus: $84.9bn, growing 18%/yr","Blood, human or animal, antisera, other blood fractions and immunological products; immunological products, put up in measured doses or in forms or packings for retail sale: $78.7bn, growing 27%/yr","Metal; precious or metal clad with precious metal, other than that of item no. 7115.10: $77.6bn, growing 67%/yr"]},{"headline":"Mexico, Canada, China take 36% of exports","detail":"Export destinations are reasonably spread, which means established routes and documentation for several markets rather than just one.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Mexico: 15.9% ($338.0bn)","Canada: 15.5% ($329.7bn)","China: 5.0% ($106.3bn)"]},{"headline":"Most imports arrive from Mexico","detail":"Mexico supplies 16% of what United States imports. If you are sourcing to sell here, that is your incumbent competition and the price you have to beat. If you are buying, those trade lanes already exist.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Mexico: 15.7% ($539.0bn)","Canada: 11.5% ($392.4bn)","China: 9.6% ($327.5bn)"]},{"headline":"2025 trade deficit of $1327.1bn","detail":"United States buys more than it sells. Deficit economies can face foreign-exchange shortages, so check currency availability and payment terms before committing.","angle":"risk","strength":"strong","evidence":["Exports $2177.1bn vs imports $3504.3bn in 2025","Exports moved 5.5% year on year"]},{"headline":"Early signal: metals; silver, unwrought, (but not powder)","detail":"Not a headline product yet, but growing 105% a year. Categories that hold that rate tend to reprice the market before they show up in the top ten, which is the window where entry is cheapest.","angle":"timing","strength":"strong","evidence":["Stone, glass & precious metals: growing 105% a year since 2022, n