tured, electric generating sets; wind-powered, (excluding those with spark-ignition or compression-ignition internal combustion piston engines)","detail":"These are the fastest-growing things South Africa buys from abroad. Rising imports mean domestic demand is outpacing domestic supply. That gap is either a place to sell into, or a place to produce locally and displace the import.","angle":"gap","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Vehicles; with only spark-ignition internal combustion reciprocating piston engine, cylinder capacity over 1000 but not over 1500cc: $2.2bn, growing 11%/yr","Metals; gold, semi-manufactured: $1.4bn, growing 44%/yr","Electric generating sets; wind-powered, (excluding those with spark-ignition or compression-ignition internal combustion piston engines): $0.6bn, growing 1139%/yr"]},{"headline":"China, Germany, United States take 29% of exports","detail":"Export destinations are reasonably spread, which means established routes and documentation for several markets rather than just one.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["China: 12.2% ($12.8bn)","Germany: 8.4% ($8.8bn)","United States: 7.9% ($8.3bn)"]},{"headline":"Most imports arrive from China","detail":"China supplies 23% of what South Africa imports. If you are sourcing to sell here, that is your incumbent competition and the price you have to beat. If you are buying, those trade lanes already exist.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["China: 23.1% ($23.6bn)","India: 7.5% ($7.6bn)","Germany: 7.1% ($7.2bn)"]},{"headline":"2025 trade surplus of $11.4bn","detail":"South Africa sells more than it buys. Surplus economies usually have foreign currency available, which makes getting paid and repatriating profit simpler.","angle":"risk","strength":"watch","evidence":["Exports $116.4bn vs imports $104.9bn in 2025","Exports moved 5.8% year on year"]},{"headline":"Early signal: vehicles; with both spark-ignition internal combustion reciprocating piston engine and electric motor for propulsion, capable of being charged by plugging to external source of electric power","detail":"Not a headline product yet, but growing 1811% a year. Categories that hold that rate tend to reprice the market before they show up in the top ten, which is the window where entry is cheapest.","angle":"timing","strength":"strong","evidence":["Transport equipment: growing 1811% a year since 2022, now 1.72% of exports at rank 16. Largest counterpart across all exports is China. Growth is uneven, so treat the projection as directional."]}]','2026-09-06 01:28:10');
