gle":"gap","strength":"strong","evidence":["Petroleum oils and oils from bituminous minerals, not containing biodiesel, not crude, not waste oils; preparations n.e.c, containing by weight 70% or more of petroleum oils or oils from bituminous minerals; not light oils and preparations: $2.7bn, growing 173%/yr","Vehicles; with only spark-ignition internal combustion reciprocating piston engine, cylinder capacity over 1500 but not over 3000cc: $0.8bn, growing 30%/yr","Oils; petroleum oils and oils obtained from bituminous minerals, crude: $0.5bn, growing 766%/yr"]},{"headline":"United Arab Emirates, India, Switzerland take 57% of exports","detail":"Export destinations are reasonably spread, which means established routes and documentation for several markets rather than just one.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["United Arab Emirates: 26.4% ($8.3bn)","India: 16.3% ($5.1bn)","Switzerland: 14.4% ($4.5bn)"]},{"headline":"Most imports arrive from China","detail":"China supplies 23% of what Ghana imports. If you are sourcing to sell here, that is your incumbent competition and the price you have to beat. If you are buying, those trade lanes already exist.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["China: 22.9% ($4.6bn)","United States: 7.1% ($1.4bn)","India: 6.9% ($1.4bn)"]},{"headline":"2025 trade surplus of $11.8bn","detail":"Ghana sells more than it buys. Surplus economies usually have foreign currency available, which makes getting paid and repatriating profit simpler.","angle":"risk","strength":"strong","evidence":["Exports $32.0bn vs imports $20.2bn in 2025","Exports moved 54.9% year on year"]},{"headline":"Services are a real part of this economy","detail":"Commercial services exports are $10.1bn, about 9% of GDP. That usually signals working payment rails, English or lingua-franca business capability, and buyers already used to contracting across borders.","angle":"entry","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Services exports $10.1bn against GDP $114.2bn (2025)"]},{"headline":"Early signal: petroleum oils and oils from bituminous minerals, not containing biodiesel, not crude, not waste oils; preparations n.e.c, containing by weight 70% or more of petroleum oils or oils from bituminous minerals; not light oils and preparations","detail":"Not a headline product yet, but growing 347% a year. Categories that hold that rate tend to reprice the market before they show up in the top ten, which is the window where entry is cheapest.","angle":"timing","strength":"strong","evidence":["Minerals & energy: growing 347% a year since 2022, now 0.54% of exports at rank 12. Largest counterpart across all exports is United Arab Emirates. Growth is uneven, so treat the projection as directional."]}]','2026-09-06 02:28:01'),('res_08c58d8382f54aca9c0377','ent_cote-divoire','run_b14745c67f9a4d5090bc92','overview','{"year":2025,"export_usd":29432666115.651,"import_usd":19583421272.797,"balance_usd":9849244842.854,"total_trade_usd":49016087388.448,"export_yoy_pct":43.23258337151827,"import_yoy_pct":13.729467330908085,"export_concentration":0.22579593099202555,"export_chapter_shares":{"10":0.0005451803927293595,"11":0.00033056249487463244,"12":0.0003621367647470444,"13":0.0001138476010917251,"14":0.0005195650725936406,"15":0.010167564709807866,"16":0.0021935946519869983,"17":0.00037172539660564367,"18":0.4033513828085103,"19":0.001678769073411735,"20":0.0003259075664538881,"21":0.006250341728920274,"22":0.00023041024263157055,"23":0.001676000469756197,"24":0.0034378757383861664,"25":0.0012484507268428102,"26":0.005581656540678433,"27":0.12579595845820427,"28":0.0004038538575573112,"29":0.00004044026488539112,"30":0.00031269667595989705,"31":0.002676349518677339,"32":0.0005867418340610277,"33":0.012232006183178153,"34":0.004792321669018605,"35":0.00002577879289014409,"36":0.000021233123310830024,"37":0.000004269618712291835,"38":0.0016698817108815375,"39":0.009940863585323156,"40":0.11848833691352655,"41":0.000006333879413693